@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;privacy] gallery-keeps-offline-changes
A pin, trash, note, tag or space change to a card MUST show on the phone at once and read
as done, online or not: it waits in the phone's copy (`data/Outbox.kt`) and reaches the
server in the background, in the order it was made, even with the app closed. A card added
to a space shows at the end of it. Waiting changes MUST go out together through the
server's push, each under its place in the queue, so the server applies a change sent
twice only once; a server without the push gets them one by one. A change the server
refuses is dropped, its card read again, and a short notice names the card or the new
space. Only while the server answers that it has no changes feed does an online change go
straight to the server. Deleting a space MUST work the same way, and so MUST making one
and saving a shared link or text once the server has taken a push, under an id the phone
makes; before that they wait for the server. A shared link the library already holds
makes way for the saved card, which keeps its own note. Waiting changes belong to the
session and are wiped at sign-out. Uploads still need a connection.
On Wi-Fi with battery to spare, the phone MUST fetch ahead the gallery pictures of Top of
Mind and the newest 1,000 cards (`data/KeptPictures.kt`) into its picture cache, which
holds up to 512 MB and is wiped at sign-out with the copy.
Source: Tavi, 22 October 2026, the plan "ThyMind: instant app and better search", step 4,
and his choice of "Pinned + newest 1,000, Wi-Fi" for the pictures; online changes queued
first for Tavi's ask of 28 October 2026 for a sync engine like Zero in Omar's Wholana, plan
"ThyMind: a Zero-style sync engine", steps 2 and 3.

